<title>SOUTH AFRICA: MALAWI TO GET FIRST LISTED COMPANY.</title>
<headline>MALAWI TO GET FIRST LISTED COMPANY.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Insurance Co Ltd (NICO) will become Malawi's first listed company on Monday, lead managers Simpson McKie James Capel said.</p>
<p>The South African investment house said in a statement proceeds from NICO's offer of 15 million ordinary shares, which closed on October 29, amounted to 30 million kwacha.</p>
<p>&quot;The share offer was significantly oversubscribed... Shares were granted to 2,300 Malawi citizens,&quot; it said. &quot;This is effectively one of the first steps in Malawi's privatisation programme.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +2711 482-1003</p>
